2026-08-27 UTC | wf_006_atacseq_chromatin_accessibility | SRR891269
Input: paired FASTQ collection; R1/R2 each 56,598,621 reads, 50 bp before trimming.
Reference: UCSC hg19 FASTA with chrM retained for explicit post-alignment filtering; BWA index built locally.
Tools: fastp 0.23.4; BWA 0.7.19-r1273; samtools 1.20; MACS2 2.2.9.1.
Preprocessing: fastp paired-end overlap detection enabled; Nextera CTGTCTCTTATACACATCT supplied for both mates; Q20 low-quality threshold; unqualified-percent limit 70; minimum post-trim length 15; N limit set to 50 (no additional N filtering for 50-bp input); poly-G trimming disabled. Passed 55,850,171 pairs; 13,396,184 reads had adapter bases trimmed.
Alignment: BWA-MEM paired-end mode (-M, -t 4, -K 5000000); secondary/supplementary records removed before name sorting. Kept complete BWA proper pairs with MAPQ >=30 on both mates and neither mate on chrM: 15,653,941 pairs.
Duplicate removal: samtools fixmate plus coordinate sort and samtools markdup -r; 8,307,534 duplicate records removed; 23,000,348 records (11,500,174 pairs) retained.
Peak calling: MACS2 callpeak, BAMPE, human effective genome size (hs), no control, q-value 0.05, --keep-dup all; narrowPeak reported 35,013 intervals.
Deliverables: final_answer/peaks.bed is the unmodified first-three-column projection of the 35,013 narrowPeak records (duplicates, if reported, preserved); final_answer/method.json declares BWA-MEM and MACS2.
